  "findings": "The regular Dutch-language route allocates 138 EC to compulsory courses, 12 EC to a selected preminor and 30 EC to open study. The classroom preminor is the first-listed illustration and has two 6 EC courses in theory and classroom research. The two other preminors cover youth assistance and children with intensive care needs. Mentoring and research participation carry no credits. The Dutch diagnostic or remedial course gates the introductory pedagogy grade, and research participation gates the observation result. Conversation Skills 2 requires Conversation Skills 1. Methodology 3 and the 12 EC thesis require completing year one. The first-year study recommendation threshold is 42 EC. Attendance and open-study approval and level rules apply.",
  "authority": "Adopted Dutch OER dated 28 May 2026, articles 9.1, 11.3–4 and 12, with the current Study Guide. The regular route has 138 EC compulsory credited study, one 12 EC preminor and 30 EC open study. The first listed classroom preminor provides 6 EC theory and 6 EC practical research. The combined Pabo route has a separate structure."
}
